# Proxy the Horizon API through this site.
#
# The browser then fetches from its own origin, which means:
#   - no CORS header needed on the upstream
#   - not blocked as mixed content, even though the upstream is http:// only
#   - no third-party relay involved at all
#
# If you deploy somewhere that does not understand this file (GitHub Pages,
# Cloudflare Pages), the site simply falls back to its relay chain - see README.

/horizon-upstream/*  http://paloma.hidencloud.com:24617/:splat  200

# Key system: /get_key/v=1, /key/auth=<auth>/c1, /key/auth=<auth>/c2 and
# /key/success=<token> are all served by the two pages below, which work out
# which step they are from location.pathname.
#
# NOTE: /key/verify/key=<KEY> and /api/key/issue are answered by middleware.js
# (Vercel Routing Middleware). A host that only reads this file cannot run it,
# so those two will fall through to key.html and 404 - see README -> Key system.

/key/*      /key.html      200
/get_key/*  /get_key.html  200
